---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Roadmap — Quire"
  description="Where DOCX stands today, XLSX in progress on the same container/lossless layer, and PPTX after that. Each format is a sibling crate in one repository."
  path="/roadmap"
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="tick">●</span> Roadmap</p>
      <h1>Three formats, one core.</h1>
      <p class="sub">
        DOCX is what works today. XLSX and PPTX will be additional crates in this same
        repository, reusing the container and round-trip layer — each with the layout
        model its format needs.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <article class="phase">
      <span class="tag now">Now</span>
      <h2>DOCX</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Lossless round-trip: the ZIP layer copies untouched entries byte-for-byte, ZIP64 and unknown extensions included — 399/399 corpus files in CI.</li>
        <li>Line breaking and pagination: Knuth-Plass optimal breaks, UAX#14 rules, CJK anywhere / Latin at whitespace.</li>
        <li>Page geometry from <code>sectPr</code>, real font-metric shaping, golden break-point snapshots.</li>
        <li>Incremental pagination with budgeted background reflow; incremental results are checked against full rebuilds.</li>
        <li>Tables with cross-page slicing, headers/footers with field substitution, style cascade, image placeholders and floating images, forced page breaks.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="phase">
      <span class="tag now">In progress</span>
      <h2>XLSX</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>A sibling crate (<code>core/xlsx</code>) on the same OPC container and round-trip gates — an 80-file XLSX corpus with per-file licensing is already collected.</li>
        <li>First the workbook model and cell parsing on the lossless layer; the formula engine follows.</li>
        <li>Charts come after the grid works, not before.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="phase">
      <span class="tag">Next</span>
      <h2>DOCX depth, then collaboration</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Tracked changes, columns (<code>w:cols</code>) and the remaining rendering gaps — each item is picked from the failure clusters the corpus comparison ranks, not from a feature calendar.</li>
        <li>The CRDT collaborative layer sits behind an adapter slot, so the collaboration dependency loads only when a document is actually shared.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="phase">
      <span class="tag">Later</span>
      <h2>PPTX</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Slide and shape model reusing the layout and shaping crates, with a canvas layout model of its own.</li>
        <li>A presentation render list on the same display-list contract the native and browser shells already consume.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="phase">
      <span class="tag">Structure</span>
      <h2>Shell split, when it makes sense</h2>
      <p>
        The shells stay in this repo until one ships its own releases, its licence
        diverges, or its contributor base diverges. Until then the layering script keeps
        the boundary clean, so a later split is moving directories rather than rewriting.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</Base>
